  <worldbody>
    <!-- <geom name="ground" type="plane" size="10 10 0.1" pos="0 0 0" quat="1 0 0 0" material="grid_mat" friction="1.0 0.005 0.01"/> -->
    <body name="base_link" pos="0 0 0.42" childclass="go2" quat="1 0 0 0">
      <camera name="follow_cam" pos="-1.5 -0 1.8" euler="0 -0.870 -1.570" mode="trackcom" />
      <!-- Matches Isaac play.py:531's video camera: cam_pos = root + [0, 2, 1],
           lookat = root. World-frame side view, 2 m off in +y, 1 m up, looking
           down at robot COM (down-tilt ≈ 26.57°).
             camera +x (image right) = world −x  →  robot facing +x renders moving left-to-right
             camera +y (image up)    = (0, −0.447, 0.894)  →  world +z roughly up after tilt
             camera −z (look dir)    = (0, −0.894, −0.447) -->
      <camera name="isaac_view" pos="0 2 1"
              xyaxes="-1 0 0   0 -0.447 0.894"
              mode="trackcom" />
      <!-- side_cam: clean horizontal side profile, tracks the robot CoM.
           Sits 2.4 m off in +y, ~0.3 m above CoM, looking level toward -y.
             camera +x (image right) = world -x  →  robot facing +x renders moving right-to-left
             camera +y (image up)    = world +z
             camera -z (look dir)    = world -y
           Good for watching the flyball hurdle jumps + wall climb in profile. -->
      <camera name="side_cam" pos="0 2.4 0.3" xyaxes="-1 0 0   0 0 1" mode="trackcom" />
      <!-- front_depth_cam: pitched 20° down to match Isaac training
           cfg depth.angle = [15, 25] (nominal 20°). NOTE: this tilt is
           cosmetic for the L00-01 / `_no_enc_loss_*` checkpoints — that
           training family disabled the depth-encoder L2 supervision, so
           the depth_image branch has no gradient signal and the
           RecurrentDepthBackbone output is empirically independent of
           the rendered depth (verified by feeding zero/near/far/random
           depth → byte-identical 32-D latent + yaw_pred). The earlier
           "horizontal workaround that lets MuJoCo walk" effect was
           actually the env_class indicator bug masquerading as a render
           gap. Keep the tilt at the training value for clarity and for
           future encoder-supervised checkpoints (P11-* etc.). xyaxes:
           right (0,-1,0), up (sin20°, 0, cos20°). -->
      <!-- 2026-07-27 pitch calibration, FINAL (supersedes the "keep 20°" note
           reverted in c84bc99, whose "floor fade ~30% from top" reading was
           taken to mean 20° — the real bags show the fade at ~56-59%).
           The REAL mount is 7.6°, NOT 20°. Measured four ways, all agreeing:
             - least-squares floor-plane fit on RAW depth, base pitch removed
               via IMU, standing frames only:
                 480x270 bag  7.60 ± 0.31°  (n=4314)   engaged 8.33 ± 1.57°
                 640x480 bag  7.28 ± 0.02°  (n= 749)   engaged 7.90 ± 1.76°
               (two different resolutions/intrinsics -> same answer; the fit
                also recovers camera height 0.35-0.40 m, which cross-validates
                it — a wrong pitch throws the height off too)
             - policy-input far-clip fraction: real 0.56-0.65 on BOTH bags;
               sim renders 0.594 at 7.6° and 0.384 at 20°.
             - ground-fade row: real ~56-59% of image height; 7.6° predicts
               56%, 20° predicts 36%.
           CONSEQUENCE (sim2sim, real obstacle h15/t20/w120, 60 Hz depth,
           noise 0.15, stereo on, 6 seeds): 20° = 6/6 clean, ZERO foot
           strikes. 7.6° = 3/6 clean, 1/6 strikes the hurdle with >=2 feet,
           one seed veers 1.25 m laterally. That is exactly the 2026-07-27
           real-run symptom, and it is why sim2sim kept passing: it rendered
           a camera geometry the robot does not have.
           ACTION: physically re-tilt the mount to the trained 20° (restores
           6/6). Keep this XML at the MEASURED 7.6° until the hardware is
           re-tilted, so sim2sim stays an honest predictor of the robot; set
           it back to 0.34202/0.93969 the moment the mount changes. -->
      <camera name="front_depth_cam" pos="0.33 0 0.08" xyaxes="0 -1 0 0.34202 0 0.93969" fovy="56.49" />
      <inertial pos="0.021112 0 -0.005366" quat="-0.000543471 0.713435 -0.00173769 0.700719"
        mass="6.921"
        diaginertia="0.107027 0.0980771 0.0244531" />
